#!/bin/busybox sh
# M3.6 USB test init. No storage drivers in this kernel. Brings up a USB CDC-ACM gadget with a shell on it and reports to /dev/kmsg;
# the timed DSS dump (dump_after) carries the report out.
export PATH=/bin
/bin/busybox --install -s /bin
mount -t proc proc /proc; mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys; mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /dev
mount -t debugfs debugfs /sys/kernel/debug 2>/dev/null
mount -t configfs configfs /sys/kernel/config
say() { echo "<6>a50-m36: $*" > /dev/kmsg; }
say "init started, Linux $(uname -r), uptime $(cut -d' ' -f1 /proc/uptime) s"
for n in 13200000.usb 131d0000.phy; do say "$n driver=$(basename "$(readlink /sys/bus/platform/devices/$n/driver 2>/dev/null)" 2>/dev/null)"; done
say "deferred: $(cat /sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred 2>/dev/null | tr '\n' ';')"
i=0; while [ $i -lt 20 ] && [ -z "$(ls /sys/class/udc 2>/dev/null)" ]; do sleep 1; i=$((i+1)); done
udc=$(ls /sys/class/udc 2>/dev/null | head -1); say "udc after ${i}s: ${udc:-NONE}"
if [ -n "$udc" ]; then
  g=/sys/kernel/config/usb_gadget/g1; mkdir -p $g/strings/0x409 $g/configs/c.1/strings/0x409 $g/functions/acm.GS0
  echo 0x1d6b > $g/idVendor; echo 0x0104 > $g/idProduct; echo 0x0200 > $g/bcdUSB
  echo "a50-test" > $g/strings/0x409/serialnumber; echo "A50 6.18" > $g/strings/0x409/manufacturer; echo "A50 ACM test" > $g/strings/0x409/product
  echo "acm" > $g/configs/c.1/strings/0x409/configuration; ln -s $g/functions/acm.GS0 $g/configs/c.1/
  # sm5713 MUIC (0x25): connect D+/D- to the SoC, the writes Samsung's com_to_usb() does. Gated on the chip's ID.
  bus=""; for a in /sys/class/i2c-adapter/i2c-*; do case "$(cat $a/name 2>/dev/null)" in *i2c-gpio*|*sm5713*) bus=${a##*i2c-};; esac; done; [ -z "$bus" ] && bus=0
  say "i2c adapters: $(for a in /sys/class/i2c-adapter/i2c-*; do echo -n "${a##*/}=$(cat $a/name) "; done) using bus $bus"
  rd() { i2cget -y $bus 0x25 $1 b 2>&1; }
  id=$(rd 0x00); ms=$(rd 0x06); cfg=$(rd 0x68)
  say "MUIC before: id=$id cntl=$(rd 0x05) manual_sw=$ms devtype1=$(rd 0x07) devtype2=$(rd 0x08) cfg1=$cfg"
  say "MUIC: switch writes disabled for this test; manual_sw=$(rd 0x06) cfg1=$(rd 0x68) cntl=$(rd 0x05)"
  echo "$udc" > $g/UDC; say "gadget bound rc=$?"
  ( while :; do [ -c /dev/ttyGS0 ] && setsid sh -c 'exec sh -i </dev/ttyGS0 >/dev/ttyGS0 2>&1'; sleep 1; done ) &
  D=/sys/kernel/debug/usb/13200000.usb
  snap() { say "SNAP $1 uptime=$(cut -d' ' -f1 /proc/uptime) mode=$(cat $D/mode 2>/dev/null) link=$(cat $D/link_state 2>/dev/null) state=$(cat /sys/class/udc/$udc/state 2>/dev/null)"
    grep -E "^(GSNPSID|GCTL|GSTS|GUSB2PHYCFG\(0\)|GUSB2I2CCTL|DCFG|DCTL|DSTS|DEVTEN|GEVNTCOUNT\(0\)|GDBGLTSSM)" $D/regdump 2>/dev/null | while IFS= read -r l; do say "REG $l"; done; }
  sleep 2; snap after-bind
  ( sleep 25; snap t+27; sleep 60; snap t+87; sleep 60; snap t+147 ) &
  j=0; last=""; while [ $j -lt 215 ]; do s=$(cat /sys/class/udc/$udc/state 2>/dev/null); sp=$(cat /sys/class/udc/$udc/current_speed 2>/dev/null)
    if [ "$s/$sp" != "$last" ]; then say "t=$(cut -d' ' -f1 /proc/uptime) udc state=$s speed=$sp"; last="$s/$sp"; fi; sleep 1; j=$((j+1)); done
fi
say "report done; waiting for the delayed dump"; while :; do sleep 60; done
